                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aadfb42f-cbba-328e-9ba9-1ec89876d177",
                        "entry_id": "6a6a093f-b575-3762-9bf5-b5cd6c236409",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tempête extratropicale, qui se déplace rapidement et qui produit de très fortes rafales descendantes en prenant la forme d’une ligne orageuse droite ayant une longue durée de vie. Ce terme s'oppose à la tornade, dont les vents tournent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cf2147c-594e-4f29-bc30-539c1e94c09b",
                                "sense_id": "aadfb42f-cbba-328e-9ba9-1ec89876d177",
                                "text": "Un derecho (« droit » en espagnol) est une tempête de vent accompagnée d’orages violents. Au contraire d’une tornade (de tornar, « tournoyer »), il progresse en ligne droite à travers un front en forme d’arc qui s’étend parfois sur 400 kilomètres. Les derechos peuvent dépasser 150 kilomètres à l’heure ; ils se déchaînent le plus souvent lors de canicules estivales, dans les vallées de l’Ohio et du Mississippi, ainsi que dans le bassin des Grands Lacs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91d6e97c-e2a6-45cb-88a6-83b0600e8cf0",
                        "source_entry_id": "6a6a093f-b575-3762-9bf5-b5cd6c236409",
                        "source_sense_id": "aadfb42f-cbba-328e-9ba9-1ec89876d177",
                        "target_lang_word": "derecho",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "derecho",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f42d21e-c336-306c-81f0-3c4ed81cbac6",
                                        "entry_id": "dd9a98a4-b4fb-3d80-a463-d9b52f35f597",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A windstorm characterized by strong, straight-line winds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53b712de-de99-4a1b-88c2-d4a3c282d9ef",
                                                "sense_id": "6f42d21e-c336-306c-81f0-3c4ed81cbac6",
                                                "text": "Combining all of the above, the Arkansas Valley, Ouachita Mountains, Interior Plateau, and Southwest Appalachian ecoregions have the greatest risk of wind damage from tornadoes and derechos, whereas weakening hurricanes are an important disturbance, especially in the Piedmont ecoregion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9dbcb3e-208c-4bb1-b321-b1e853c2a294",
                                                "sense_id": "6f42d21e-c336-306c-81f0-3c4ed81cbac6",
                                                "text": "Derechos have winds as powerful as those of some hurricanes and tornadoes. \"Derecho\" comes from the Spanish word meaning \"straight.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c00099bd-eb2b-48a8-ad1a-25d696358690",
                                                "sense_id": "6f42d21e-c336-306c-81f0-3c4ed81cbac6",
                                                "text": "A derecho can be as destructive as a weak to moderate tornado, but the damage is mainly the result of straight-line rather than rotating winds.\nHowever, tornadoes can also form along the bow of a derecho. Derechos can sometimes be recognized as a bank of ominous-looking \"shelf\" clouds that appear darker than normal clouds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
